1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,752
The knight on g four is not hanging by accident.

2
00:00:04,912 --> 00:00:09,365
The Ruy Lopez gives both sides fast development.

3
00:00:09,525 --> 00:00:13,977
Black jumps in with a move that dares White to capture.

4
00:00:14,137 --> 00:00:18,590
White opens the center while the king is safe.

5
00:00:18,750 --> 00:00:23,203
That pawn push looks like a free knight.

6
00:00:23,363 --> 00:00:27,815
But the h pawn is part of the fishing pole.

7
00:00:27,975 --> 00:00:32,428
White takes the bait and removes the knight.

8
00:00:32,587 --> 00:00:37,040
Black recaptures and opens the g file immediately.

9
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:41,652
The queen arrives with a dangerous attack on h four.

10
00:00:41,812 --> 00:00:46,265
Material is not the only thing hanging in this position.

11
00:00:46,425 --> 00:00:50,877
The practical lesson is to ask what the bait attacks.

12
00:00:51,037 --> 00:00:55,650
Would you grab the knight?

